# ============================================================================
# R2 API Credentials Configuration
# ============================================================================
#
# This file is a template. To use it:
#   1. Copy this file: cp .env.example .env
#   2. Fill in your actual credentials in .env
#   3. Never commit .env to git (it's in .gitignore)
#
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How to Create R2 API Credentials
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. Go to Cloudflare Dashboard (https://dash.cloudflare.com)
# 2. Navigate to: R2 → Manage R2 API Tokens
# 3. Click "Create API Token"
# 4. Choose "User API Token" (recommended for personal/development use)
#    - Use "Account API Token" only for production systems with multiple users
#
# 5. Configure the token:
#    - Token Name: Something descriptive (e.g., "r2-email-viewer-token")
#    - Permissions: Choose based on your needs:
#      * "Admin Read & Write" - Full access (read and delete emails)
#      * "Admin Read" - Read-only access (view emails only)
#    - TTL (Time to Live): Choose expiration or "Forever" for convenience
#
# 6. Click "Create" and copy the credentials shown (you'll only see them once!)
#
# 7. Fill in the values below in your .env file (not this .env.example file)
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# R2 Access Key ID
# Example: XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-access-key-id-here

# R2 Secret Access Key
# Example: XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-secret-access-key-here

# R2 Endpoint URL (jurisdiction-specific)
# Format: https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# Example: https://XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
R2_ENDPOINT=https://your-account-id.r2.cloudflarestorage.com

# ============================================================================
# Additional Notes
# ============================================================================
#
# Security Best Practices:
#   - Keep .env file secure and never commit it to version control
#   - Rotate credentials periodically for better security
#   - Use read-only permissions if you don't need to delete emails
#   - If credentials are compromised, revoke and create new token immediately
#
# To Revoke/Rotate Token:
#   1. Go to Cloudflare Dashboard → R2 → Manage R2 API Tokens
#   2. Find your token and click "Delete"
#   3. Create a new token and update your .env file
#
# Loading Environment Variables:
#   After creating your .env file, load it with:
#   $ set -a; source .env; set +a
#
#   Or if using the virtual environment with auto-load configured:
#   $ source .venv/bin/activate  # Automatically loads .env
#
# ============================================================================
